                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b3732766-706a-3cd8-94e4-43fe8bca3b09",
                        "entry_id": "8665857b-cf61-37e4-88d9-6d9ff0a1d08d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "gezellig, prettig in de omgang, een aangename indruk makend"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7e48dbe-5660-495a-871b-5a1b65309404",
                                "sense_id": "b3732766-706a-3cd8-94e4-43fe8bca3b09",
                                "text": "Heh ! die zee! — hoorde ik een welgekleeden badgast zuchtend zeggen, dien ik al meermalen aan het strand ontmoet had, waardoor wij allengs in gesprek waren gekomen; een van die gesprekken, die tot de opvoeding behooren en hem, die ze goed heeft leeren voeren, levenslang door de wereld kunnen helpen met den naam van een sociabel mensch, zonder dat de andere sociabele menschen bemerken of zoo iemand iets weet en iets beduidt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1882d8cc-42a1-46b4-ab89-e05e25ae1c7c",
                                "sense_id": "b3732766-706a-3cd8-94e4-43fe8bca3b09",
                                "text": "Geen aanleiding, het is een menselijke kwestie. Dat is trouwens een van de redenen waarom Club al 6 of 7 jaar geen kampioen is. Ze zijn niet sociabel, ze vergeten de menselijke kant. Ik heb nog nooit iemand ontmoet die zegt dat hij een vriend is van Vincent Man­naert. Hij is kil. Ik heb de indruk dat hij niet gelukkig is. Terwijl ik me amuseer in het voetbal.’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "17e6e2b3-e963-4406-97a4-1e83b71ded82",
                        "source_entry_id": "8665857b-cf61-37e4-88d9-6d9ff0a1d08d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b3732766-706a-3cd8-94e4-43fe8bca3b09",
                        "target_lang_word": "pleasant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "pleasant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                        "entry_id": "59dd0335-ac27-3032-a14f-ea12079b6db9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Giving pleasure; pleasing in manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4e14490-ff1d-46e2-9861-502fa4c4088b",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "We had a pleasant walk around the town."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18ebccf2-52fa-44a0-8285-4be206877765",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "It wasn't so hot outside, but pleasant enough to have lunch in the garden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4fc8373-7ea2-4c5c-a823-6f36c5fb58c9",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "Behold, how good and pleasant it is for brethren to dwell together in unity!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb1ed354-8692-406f-8f48-2af4c7de5b4a",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "“I cannot see that London has any great advantage over the country, for my part, except the shops and public places. The country is a vast deal pleasanter, is not it, Mr. Bingley?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7933792-ad8f-4723-afae-6aee98e87a21",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "“I was only going to say,” said Scrooge’s nephew, “that the consequence of his taking a dislike to us, and not making merry with us, is, as I think, that he loses some pleasant moments, which could do him no harm. I am sure he loses pleasanter companions than he can find in his own thoughts, either in his mouldy old office, or his dusty chambers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40270d6d-493a-417d-8b63-3939ca96a282",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "“O Oysters, come and walk with us!” / The Walrus did beseech. / “A pleasant walk, a pleasant talk, / Along the briny beach:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf751f44-b49e-4df5-852c-b19fee83b593",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "It was a joy to snatch some brief respite, and find himself in the rectory drawing–room. Listening here was as pleasant as talking; just to watch was pleasant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50f07bd5-1073-45ee-a305-3babb9fcb62a",
                                                "sense_id": "1600659e-0f9d-3111-a19f-55edc06d6fa1",
                                                "text": "“[…] If you pray to St. Anne before twelve o’clock on a Wednesday, you’ll get a pleasant surprise before the end of the week.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9a2852b2-da9e-3136-8343-2b1c38cce2ca",
                                        "entry_id": "59dd0335-ac27-3032-a14f-ea12079b6db9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Facetious, joking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79712a15-5642-4400-88c5-962256d639ab",
                                                "sense_id": "9a2852b2-da9e-3136-8343-2b1c38cce2ca",
                                                "text": "[T]ell the pleasant prince this mock of his / Hath turn’d his balls to gun-stones […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09f5bd0b-fbff-4101-adaa-50281fc4f70c",
                                                "sense_id": "9a2852b2-da9e-3136-8343-2b1c38cce2ca",
                                                "text": "[…] I present you here with a merrie conceited Comedie, called the Shoomakers Holyday, acted by my Lorde Admiralls Players this present Christmasse, before the Queenes most excellent Maiestie. For the mirth and pleasant matter, by her Highnesse graciously accepted; being indeede no way offensiue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "pleasant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8633462b-b430-3f9b-8ea0-7b3beed58a30",
                                        "entry_id": "0b42b888-94df-36fd-ad79-369ae1635114",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wit; a humorist; a buffoon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "586c0c54-bfd6-46ed-8b9f-18342f9c5f0c",
                                                "sense_id": "8633462b-b430-3f9b-8ea0-7b3beed58a30",
                                                "text": "[…] Galba was no better than one of the buffons or pleasants that professe to make folke merry and to laugh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e9a0381-7119-4020-8274-5b14abcd2866",
                                                "sense_id": "8633462b-b430-3f9b-8ea0-7b3beed58a30",
                                                "text": "1696, uncredited translator, The General History of the Quakers by Gerard Croese, London: John Dunton, Book 2, p. 96,\nYea, in the Courts of Kings and Princes, their Fools, and Pleasants, which they kept to relax them from grief and pensiveness, could not show themselves more dexterously ridiculous, than by representing the Quakers, or aping the motions of their mouth, voice, gesture, and countenance:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
